# pygame-ce — precompiled aarch64 wheel pin, for the INSTALLER image only. Phase 5/6 of
# .claude/plans/internal-install.plan.md.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT UNDER packages/. Every `packages/*/prebuilt.pin` is auto-discovered by
# rootfs/customize-base.sh and extracted into the RELEASE base. This one is 39 MB of Python SDL
# bindings that only install/ui uses, and install/ui does not ship on the release image at all —
# so it would be pure weight on every device. install/mkroot.sh (Phase 6) reads it instead, using
# the same field names so the parsing idiom is shared.
#
# WHY A WHEEL AT ALL, rather than a repo package or an overlay build. Measured against the pinned
# builder, 2026-08-22: **there is no `python-pygame` in the holo repos, and no `PySDL2` either.**
# There is not even a plain `sdl2` — only `sdl2-compat`, `sdl2_ttf`, `sdl2_image` and `sdl3`. The
# plan asserted the opposite ("all already built by the overlay ... so no new package work") and
# mkroot.sh would have discovered otherwise. The alternatives were a from-source overlay package
# (SDL2 + Cython + a compiled extension in the build) or a ctypes shim of our own; the wheel is
# the one that needed no new build and no new code.
#
# WHAT MADE IT ACCEPTABLE, since a wheel vendors its own libraries and that is normally a reason to
# refuse one. All checked before use:
#   - it bundles libSDL2 2.32.10 with the **wayland** video driver compiled in (dummy/offscreen
#     too), and dlopens only libwayland-client/cursor/egl, libxkbcommon, libgbm — every one of
#     which this image already carries for gamescope. It does NOT need X11 or Xwayland.
#   - cp313 matches the image's Python exactly (3.13.7); a Python bump invalidates this pin, which
#     is the point of pinning it.
#   - manylinux_2_17 / glibc 2.17 baseline, well under what the image ships.
#   - the sha256 below is PyPI's own published digest for the file, re-verified after download.
#
# HW-PROVEN, 2026-08-22 on an AYANEO Pocket S2: unzipped into tmpfs, PYTHONPATH'd, and driven by
# install/installer-session — gamescope as root with no logind session, our UI as its only client
# at 2560x1440 on Wayland, the §4d consent screen drawn from real facts, both pads enumerated, and
# the sequence completed on the panel by hand.
#
# THE FILE IS A ZIP, NOT A TARBALL. mkroot.sh must unzip it into the installer rootfs'
# site-packages (/usr/lib/python3.13/site-packages/) — `strip` below is 0 because a wheel's members
# are already rooted at the package directory (pygame/, pygame_ce.libs/, *.dist-info/). It carries
# its own libraries, so it needs no `deps:` row.
#
# To bump: pick a release at https://pypi.org/project/pygame-ce/#files, take the
# cp<PY>-manylinux…aarch64 wheel matching the image's Python, and set version + url + sha256
# together. Verify the vendored SDL still has wayland:
#   unzip -p <whl> 'pygame_ce.libs/libSDL2-2-*.so*' > /tmp/sdl.so && strings /tmp/sdl.so | grep -x wayland
name: pygame-ce
version: 2.5.8
# The path is CONTENT-HASHED by PyPI -- it cannot be constructed from the package name and
# version, only read from https://pypi.org/pypi/pygame-ce/<version>/json. Verified 200 on
# 2026-08-22.
url: https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/4d/fe/4be67df98bb05f7b024900f80fe4d07a72cec7022262d17c449b2a9f6034/pygame_ce-2.5.8-cp313-cp313-manylinux2014_aarch64.manylinux_2_17_aarch64.whl
sha256: e3183bc0d808e739ca2400df45a5bfae10704ccbcacab0f04f9adc9027e86427
kind: zip
strip: 0
dest: /usr/lib/python3.13/site-packages
python: cp313
